// stdlib/ext4: ext2 and ext4 images made by mke2fs -d (e2fsprogs 1.47.4) read: inodes, extents, indirect blocks, holes, symlinks, checksums. Then written and read back: on the ext2 image, files through direct, single, double and triple indirect blocks, truncation, mkdir/rename/rmdir/link/unlink/symlinks, inodes running out; on the ext4 image (metadata_csum), extent trees growing a level and splitting a leaf, truncation, directory blocks with checksums, renames, the vfs, a full disk; on a third image with a journal (see JRN_IMG), recovery of four transactions (escaped block, revoke), an htree directory written to, an extent tree of depth 2, a damaged commit block, needs_recovery without a journal.
// e2fsck -fn (e2fsprogs 1.47.4, WSL) on the three images as this test leaves them, and on the states holding the triple-indirect file, the split leaf and the depth-2 tree: clean, exit code 0, no messages (Nov 17). The writes run through C (fid ccompile): fid run passes the ext2 part, then runs out of memory (docs/reference/stdlib-agent-bugs.md, bug 20).
// Expected output:
// ext2 "fides-e2": block 1024, 128 blocks, 24 inodes, 1 groups, inode size 256, metadata_csum false
// ls /: lost+found big.txt docs hello.txt link longlink sparse.bin
// /hello.txt: Hello from ext2!
// /big.txt: 15360 bytes, block 0 "block 00", block 12 (single indirect) "block 12", block 14 "block 14"
// /sparse.bin: 20480 bytes, hole byte 1000 = 0, byte 6144 = 99, non-zero bytes 960
// /link -> hello.txt, read through it: Hello from ext2!
// /longlink: 79 byte target (slow symlink), following it: ENOENT
// /docs/../docs/readme: doc
// ext4 "fides-e4": block 1024, 256 blocks, 48 inodes, 64-bit descriptors 64, metadata_csum true, superblock checksum ok
// every inode checksum ok: true
// /sparse.bin: 6 extents (tree depth 1), logical 0 3 6 9 12 15, same bytes as on ext2: true
// /many: 19 entries, first file_with_a_fairly_long_name_number_1
// vfs /mnt/docs/readme: doc, /mnt/link: Hello from ext2!, ls /mnt/docs: readme
// corrupted inode 15: checksum ok false, vfs stat EIO
// unknown feature: unsupported incompat features 8000
// bad magic: bad magic
// ext2 writable true, 77 free blocks, 6 free inodes
// create /new.txt: ok, reads written on ext2
// /grow.bin: 15 blocks through the single indirect block, i_blocks 32, same bytes true
// /far.bin: size 67383310, 7 blocks (2 data, 2 for the double tree, 3 for the triple), read back "dind" "tind", hole byte 0
//   truncated to 1000: 0 blocks left, i_blocks 0
// mkdir /dir2: ok, links of / 5
// rename /dir2/a -> /docs/a2: ok, /docs/a2 reads A
// rename /dir2 -> /docs/dir2: ok, .. is /docs true, links / 4 /docs 3
// rename /docs into itself: EINVAL, rmdir /docs: ENOTEMPTY, unlink /docs: EISDIR
// hard link /hello2.txt: ok, links 2, reads Hello from ext2!
// unlink /big.txt: 16 blocks freed (15 data + 1 indirect), lookup ENOENT
// symlinks: /short -> docs/a2 reads A, /long (82 bytes, slow) reads A
// rmdir /docs/dir2: ok, links /docs 2, 74 free blocks, 1 free inodes
// created until ENOSPC: 1 files
// reopened: lost+found short docs hello.txt link longlink sparse.bin new.txt grow.bin far.bin hello2.txt long; 74 free blocks, 1 free inodes; bad inode checksums 0, bitmap/count mismatches 0, groups say 74/1 free
//   /docs: readme a2
// ext4 writable true, 180 free blocks, 10 free inodes
// /frag.bin: 9 extents, depth 1, i_blocks 20, block 16 reads x16
// /split.bin: 90 extents, depth 1, root entries 2, tree blocks 2, i_blocks 184, byte at 178K+1 s
//   truncated to 100 KiB: 50 extents, depth 1, i_blocks 102
// /frag.bin overwritten and appended: xYZ / tail, 10 extents, size 18436
// /many: 25 entries in 2 blocks, added_..._5 reads 5
// rename /many/file_with_a_fairly_long_name_number_1 -> /renamed: ok, replace /hello.txt by /renamed: ok, /hello.txt reads 1
// vfs: mkdir ok, write ok, rename ok, truncate ok, reads through, rmdir ok, unlink ok
// fill: wrote 111 KiB of 400, free blocks 0, another write ENOSPC, extents 2, same bytes true
// after unlinking them: -7 blocks from the start
// reopened: superblock checksum true, 173 free blocks, 5 free inodes; bad inode checksums 0, bitmap/count mismatches 0, groups say 173/5 free
//   /: lost+found big.txt docs hello.txt longlink many sparse.bin v.txt
// journal image without recovery: writable false (the journal needs recovery (opened without replaying it)), write EROFS, /note.txt journal test
// recovered: true, 4 transactions, 3 blocks replayed, 1 revoked, bad checksums 0, writable true
//   /note.txt replayed by t, block 2000 c03b39986573 (escaped magic restored), block 2002 00000000 (revoked), block 2003 third transaction
//   journal start 0, sequence 6, needs_recovery false, second open recovers again false
// /big: indexed true, 70 entries
//   after a create and an unlink: indexed false, 70 entries, entry_with_a_long_name_70 reads f70, added reads added to an htree directory
// /deep.bin: 400 extents, depth 2, tree blocks 6, 406 blocks used, byte at 798K d
//   truncated to 300 KiB: 150 extents, depth 1, 152 blocks used
// reopened: recovered false, 1713 free blocks, 41 free inodes; bad inode checksums 0, bitmap/count mismatches 0, groups say 1713/41 free
// bad commit checksum in transaction 4: 3 transactions, 2 blocks, block 2003 00000000, /note.txt replayed by t
// needs_recovery without a journal: needs journal recovery: no journal
